; fake-igd - what SELinux needs for fake-igd that the system's policy does not say (1.7.7, as otp's
; otp_server.cil). Installed by install.sh and by every upgrade (semodule -i fake_igd_server.cil), taken
; away with semodule -r fake_igd_server. Labels first; a narrow rule only where no label or boolean does
; it, each in a block of its own.
;
; fake-igd.service and fake-igd-api.service run as unconfined_service_t (a program of /opt started by
; systemd): their own ports - 1900/udp, the SOAP port, the API on 127.0.0.1, SNMP - need no label. What is
; confined is nginx and php-fpm (httpd_t): the pages ask the API on 127.0.0.1 (the boolean
; httpd_can_network_connect, set by install.sh and Settings → SELinux) and read its token.
;
; /run/fake-igd-api holds the API's token and port. The pages (php-fpm, httpd_t) read them; made by
; systemd as var_run_t, httpd_t may not read it. Labelled as the web server's own run files, which httpd_t
; reads; the API (unconfined_service_t) writes it as before. The command line's key beside them
; (cli-token) is 0600 the API's account's: the label lets the pages nothing the file's mode refuses.
;
; Both spellings: the policy reads a path through file_contexts.subs_dist first - on RHEL 8 "/run" is
; looked up as "/var/run", on newer policies the other way round - so a rule for one of them alone may
; never be matched. The one never looked up does nothing.
(filecon "/run/fake-igd-api" dir (system_u object_r httpd_var_run_t ((s0) (s0))))
(filecon "/run/fake-igd-api/.*" any (system_u object_r httpd_var_run_t ((s0) (s0))))
(filecon "/var/run/fake-igd-api" dir (system_u object_r httpd_var_run_t ((s0) (s0))))
(filecon "/var/run/fake-igd-api/.*" any (system_u object_r httpd_var_run_t ((s0) (s0))))

; systemd hands /run/fake-igd-api back to the service's account before every command of the unit
; (RuntimeDirectory=): it may change the owner and the mode of what is in it. Under enforcing that was
; refused to otp as "init_t -> httpd_var_run_t file { setattr }". Only that: no read, no write. In a block
; of its own, so that a policy without one of the types still takes the rest of the module.
(optional fake_igd_server_systemd_runtime
    (allow init_t httpd_var_run_t (dir (getattr setattr search open read)))
    (allow init_t httpd_var_run_t (file (getattr setattr))))
